				function rawContent() {
					return "\nAbsence Management in Oracle Fusion HCM handles leave policies, accrual calculations, and absence tracking for your organization.\n\n## Absence Architecture\n\nKey components of absence management:\n- Leave types: Paid time off, sick leave, etc.\n- Accrual policies: How leave is earned\n- Carryover rules: Unused leave handling\n- Absence requests: Employee leave submission\n\n## Leave Types\n\nDefine leave categories for your organization:\n\n### Statutory Leave\n- Vacation: Paid time off\n- Sick Leave: Illness-related absence\n- Bereavement: Death-related leave\n- Parental: Birth or adoption leave\n\n### Administrative Leave\n- Training: Professional development\n- Jury Duty: Legal obligation\n- Military Service: Military reserve\n- Unpaid Leave: Without compensation\n\n## Accrual Policies\n\nDefine how leave is earned:\n\n### Accrual Methods\n- Service-based: Increases with years\n- Fixed: Same amount for all\n- Fixed Anniversary: Resets each anniversary\n- Scheduled: Varies by date\n\n### Accrual Calculation\nAccruals run automatically:\n- Monthly: Accrue each month\n- Quarterly: Accrue each quarter\n- Annually: Accrue each anniversary\n- As-needed: Manual accrual\n\n## Carryover Rules\n\nManage unused leave:\n\n### Carryover Policies\n- No carryover: Lose unused balance\n- Limited carryover: Maximum carry forward\n- Full carryover: Carry all unused\n- Decay: Reduce carryover over time\n\n## Request Management\n\nEmployee leave request workflow:\n\n### Request Process\n1. **Submission**: Employee submits request\n2. **Validation**: System checks availability\n3. **Approval**: Manager reviews and approves\n4. **Deduction**: Balance automatically adjusted\n5. **Payroll**: Marked in payroll system\n\n### Approval Rules\n- Manager approval required\n- Multiple approval levels\n- Auto-approval for eligible requests\n- Exception handling for edge cases\n\n## Entitlements\n\nManage employee leave entitlements:\n\n### Entitlement Components\n- Base entitlement: Standard allocation\n- Adjustments: Special grants or corrections\n- Carryover: From previous period\n- Current balance: Available for use\n\n## Absence Reporting\n\nTrack and report on absence:\n\n### Reports Generated\n- Absence Summary: Total by employee\n- Leave Balance: Current available\n- Absence Trends: Historical patterns\n- Audit Trail: Change history\n\n## Compliance Considerations\n\nEnsure regulatory compliance:\n- Statutory minimums: Meet legal requirements\n- Portability: Correct state regulations\n- Disclosure: Proper accounting treatment\n- Records: Maintain audit trail\n\n## Integration with Payroll\n\nAbsence data affects payroll:\n- Hours adjustment: Time not worked\n- Earnings calculation: Leave paid as earnings\n- Deduction: Balance reduction\n- Accrual: Ongoing tracking\n\n## Multi-Country Considerations\n\nManaging global leave requirements:\n- Country-specific rules\n- Local statutory minimums\n- Currency and payment treatment\n- Reporting requirements\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Establish clear policies** documented for employees\n2. **Configure policies** matching legal requirements\n3. **Test accruals** thoroughly before go-live\n4. **Communicate changes** to affected employees\n5. **Monitor usage** for patterns and issues\n\n## Conclusion\n\nProper absence management ensures fair treatment, legal compliance, and accurate payroll processing. Invest in thorough policy definition and system configuration.\n";
				}
